#: ../../source/index.rst:5
#: 89870c5eb94b464a906ffdcc42f4cd8a
msgid "Welcome to the ArduPilot Development Site"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:9
#: ddaccab5631a4f95a823ee45e0702015
msgid "Keep up with the latest ArduPilot related blogs on `ArduPilot.org! <https://ardupilot.org/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:11
#: 4316dc98101a46b99bf60072fa488c30
msgid ":ref:`ArduPilot <ardupilot:home>` is the leading open source autopilot system supporting multi-copters, traditional helicopters, fixed wing aircraft, rovers, submarines and antenna trackers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:14
#: 592a4c754da74466a7477cecc67b3c73
msgid "We pride ourselves on being **versatile** (rich in features with support for a large number of flight controllers, sensors and frame types), **trusted** (reliable and predictable) and **open** (both in terms of software and in our team's organisation and governance)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:16
#: d1af8074cc014986accd1284f147a7eb
msgid "The source code is developed by a group of volunteer and professional (i.e. paid) developers who, along with our users and `Partners <https://ardupilot.org/about/Partners>`__, make up the `ArduPilot Community <https://ardupilot.org>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:19
#: c2b960d030054d50bea834e6877a1e03
msgid "Getting Involved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:21
#: 4b1920a270fa4abd8bf41a587d43e8c5
msgid "New developers are always welcome! The best way to start is to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:23
#: a83f4b1e30ff4307865fea8bca623d57
msgid "read this wiki to learn the basics of the software and :ref:`how the team works <how-the-team-works>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:24
#: 45aa0439bed44b198db7286ac84428df
msgid "get involved with the other developers by posting on the `Developer Team Forum <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/c/development-team>`__, chat to us on `ArduPilot Discord Chat <https://ardupilot.org/discord>`__ or join the :ref:`weekly development call <ardupilot-discord-server>`.  You can also find a large number of users and some developers in the `ArduPilot facebook group <https://www.facebook.com/groups/ArduPilot.org>`__.  :ref:`All channels <common-contact-us>` are open to all.  Lurk for a while to get a feel for it, then participate!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:25
#: 527e64b71f4449a69d2c3a3e5a045b94
msgid "find a specific bug you'd like to fix or a feature you'd like to add (check out the `good first issues <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22>`__, recent `issues from Randy <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/issues/created_by/rmackay9>`__ or our :ref:`roadmap <roadmap>` for ideas).  Please do not ask to be assigned an issue; just work on it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:26
#: 9aaa5e01f7984e48bf425b68a05a7d6a
msgid "if there is already a related pull request you can review it and join the discussion there, otherwise fix the bug in your own clone and :ref:`test <simulation-2>` that it's working"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:27
#: 01143a965b174989b1974b03fd9135ba
msgid "submit the change to the main code base :ref:`via a pull request <submitting-patches-back-to-master>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:30
#: f147480372a24142a62efaf64a4f14e2
msgid "Why the name?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:32
#: 9d4738e2c6e44a5dabb30308df281859
msgid "The 'Ardu' part of the ArduPilot name comes from `Arduino <http://www.arduino.cc/>`__. The original :ref:`APM1 and APM2 <common-apm25-and-26-overview>` boards were based around the Arduino development environment and AVR CPUs. We long ago outgrew these boards so we recommend users use one of the many more capable boards found on our :ref:`Autopilot Hardware Options page <common-autopilots>` including the Pixhawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:35
#: bd59fe04fd944ef08b89cc7f9eb7e966
msgid "A timeline history of ArduPilot can be found :ref:`here <history-of-ardupilot>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:38
#: d3159aeb9892488cbddd8cebdb20a141
msgid "Supported boards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:40
#: 687d1f9f68d040b0821251d263c06a10
msgid "The :ref:`Autopilot Hardware Options <common-autopilots>` page provides an overview for all the supported controller boards, including :ref:`Pixhawk <common-pixhawk-overview>`, :ref:`The Cube <common-thecube-overview>`, :ref:`Pixracer <common-pixracer-overview>`, :ref:`NAVIO2 <common-navio2-overview>`, :ref:`Bebop2 <copter:parrot-bebop-autopilot>`, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:44
#: 0d8f0c7e2ee04258b657b2cb87c47285
msgid "To get going quickly please consider purchasing one of the :ref:`ready-to-fly vehicles <common-rtf>` including the very low-cost `SkyRocket/SkyViper drone <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/skyrocket.html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:46
#: f00b0ec494534637b7bbb788d687a833
msgid "The ArduPilot source code includes the `AP-HAL <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_HAL>`__ Hardware Abstraction Layer, making it relatively easy to port the code to a wide range of autopilot boards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:51
#: 85d347aaa570406d90880aa184347233
msgid "Project List"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:53
#: 89b1600370c64b509e08b0c4acdd62c8
msgid "The ArduPilot system is made up of (or relies upon) several different projects which are listed below.  Those marked with an asterix (\\*) are peer projects that have their own owners outside the core ArduPilot dev team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:58
#: d4264041ca754446be85e7906d269695
msgid "Plane (:ref:`wiki <plane:home>`, `code <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot>`__) - autopilot for planes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:61
#: 451f238b9ea84825a26f76dc084ee679
msgid "Copter (:ref:`wiki <copter:home>`, `code <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot>`__) - autopilot for multicopters and traditional helicopters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:64
#: 6d0f3bd9d3af486eac78764570c9e480
msgid "Rover (:ref:`wiki <rover:home>`, `code <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot>`__) - autopilot for ground vehicles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:67
#: b54280f361a24f878b97a2ac301091ca
msgid "Sub (:ref:`wiki <sub:home>`, `code <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot>`__) - autopilot for submersible vehicles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:70
#: b8246fa276af414fa9cc531f1e0e770f
msgid "Antenna Tracker (:ref:`wiki <antennatracker:home>`, `code <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot>`__) - for automatically aiming an antenna at a vehicle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:72
#: 4a8fa13cc33147898da1e4859198f304
msgid "Mission Planner (:ref:`wiki <planner:home>`, `code <https://github.com/ArduPilot/MissionPlanner>`__) - the most commonly used ground station written in C# for windows but also runs on Linux and MacOS via mono"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:76
#: a84ad991e2114cecba33f5860f227005
msgid "APM Planner 2.0 (:ref:`wiki <planner2:home>`, `code <https://github.com/ArduPilot/apm_planner>`__) is a ground station specifically for APM written in C++ using the Qt libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:79
#: 46a4ecea26be495e990d82a71bf02443
msgid ":ref:`MAVProxy <mavproxy:home>` - command line oriented and scriptable ground station (mostly used by developers)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:81
#: b9bb6027e5a640c8852f53d8423b094f
msgid "`DroneKit <http://dronekit.io/>`__ - APM SDK for apps running on vehicles, mobile devices and/or in the cloud."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:82
#: 6400d391abf444569099fd4d26c48a3f
msgid "MinimOSD (`wiki <http://code.google.com/p/arducam-osd/wiki/minimosd>`__, `code <https://github.com/diydrones/MinimOSD-Extra>`__) - on-screen display of flight data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:85
#: 0e4a23430af94a568105a5372b995906
msgid "Tower (`wiki <https://github.com/DroidPlanner/Tower/wiki>`__, `code <https://github.com/DroidPlanner/Tower>`__, `google play <https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=org.droidplanner.android>`__) - android ground station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:88
#: a87250f8fd3a4fbfa19ee28e1c22f439
msgid "`QGroundControl* <http://www.qgroundcontrol.org/>`__ is an alternative ground station written in C++ using the Qt libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:89
#: a5f67344ce3240739c765c4922b926f6
msgid "`PX4* <https://pixhawk.org/start>`__ - designers of the original PX4FMU hardware (from which the Pixhawk was developed)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:90
#: 80adeca5359c4abbbe9a855ef0a236fb
msgid "`MAVLink* <https://mavlink.io>`__ - the protocol for communication between the ground station, flight controller and some peripherals including the OSD. A \"Dummy's Guide\" to working with MAVLink is `here <https://diydrones.com/group/arducopterusergroup/forum/mavlink-tutorial-for-absolute-dummies-part-i>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:95
#: 1cf887f1a1a940faa5c431c8123f07e3
msgid "`DroneCAN* <https://dronecan.github.io/>`__ - Lightweight protocol designed for reliable communication in aerospace and robotic applications via CAN bus. ArduPilot is using the `libcanard <https://github.com/DroneCAN/libcanard>`__, which is a portable, cross-platform library written in C++ with minimal dependency on the C++ standard library and calls its version DroneCAN, allowing UAVCAN to evolve separately."
msgstr ""

